{code}

This is your owner key. binference shows it only now and keeps only its public half. Write it down and keep it offline, such as in a password manager.

The owner key raises a wallet's ceiling, saves addresses the agent may pay, exports a wallet and attaches a new machine. If you lose it, your wallets keep working inside their ceiling, but none of that works any more: use your rescue address to empty them, then set up again with a new owner key.
